  "solution": {
    "text": "From relation,&nbsp;<math><mrow><mtext>E</mtext> <mo>=</mo> <mi>ρ</mi> <mtext>J</mtext></mrow></math>, the magnitude of the electric field is greater in the right rod as compared to the left rod. Therefore the magnitude of the potential gradient in the right rod is greater. (Remember that potential is continuous).<br />Therefore the variation is shown by the following figure.<br /><br /><img alt=\"\" height=\"139\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/content_15.20.2..png\" width=\"207\" />",
